# Narrow ignores for ChromaDB CVEs with no upstream patched release.
# Locked version is chromadb 1.5.9 (pyproject floor is >=1.1.1; Trivy may
# report the floor). Advisories list affected <=1.5.9 and patched: none.
# Latest stable is still 1.5.9 (2026-05-05); 1.5.10 exists only as a
# development build. OpenFatture uses chromadb.PersistentClient locally
# (openfatture/ai/rag/vector_store.py) and never starts or connects to a
# ChromaDB HTTP server, so the server-API attack surface does not apply.
# Revisit when chroma-core/chroma ships a release that lists a
# first_patched_version for these IDs.
#
# Pre-existing on main (same chromadb 1.5.9). Flagged on the aiohttp
# 3.14.4 lockfile bump because the uv.lock diff was large enough for
# GitHub code scanning to treat lockfile alerts as new.
#
# CVE-2026-45829 / GHSA-f4j7-r4q5-qw2c (CRITICAL)
# Pre-auth code injection via trust_remote_code on /api/v2 collections.
# Reason: unfixable upstream (patched: none through 1.5.9); not exposed
# (local PersistentClient only; remote model-code execution is not enabled).
CVE-2026-45829 exp:2027-01-21
GHSA-f4j7-r4q5-qw2c exp:2027-01-21
#
# CVE-2026-45833 / GHSA-36p7-vc44-83pf (CRITICAL)
